==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Ancient Shafts can be found by defeating [[Guardian]]s or within chests in [[Ancient Shrine]]s. They are also sold by the travelling merchant [[Teli]], who can be found on the path northwest of [[Hateno Village]]. Like other [[Ancient Material]]s, they were made 10,000 years ago to be used in the [[Ancient Technology]] of the [[Sheikah]]. They are made of a sturdy, yet unknown material.<ref name="Inventory"/>

During the [[Side Quest]] "[[Slated for Upgrades]]", [[Link]] can give [[Purah]] three Ancient Shafts to upgrade his [[Remote Bomb]]s [[Rune]]s.<ref>{{Cite|You'll need {{Color BotW|Red|three ancient shafts}} to power up your {{Color BotW|Blue|Remote Bombs}}.|Purah|BotW}}</ref> The [[Ancient Oven]] in the Akkala Ancient Tech Lab also requires Ancient Shafts to make certain pieces of [[Ancient Soldier Gear]]. They can be used to make [[Gray Dye]] at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]] or exchanged for [[Mon]] at the [[Fang and Bone]].

Ancient Shafts are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]].

{{Material Armors|BotW|Ancient Shaft}}

